# UI test: `e?` where `e` is not nullable (SC0530).
#
# Always true, so it is never what anyone meant — the argument `SC0520` makes
# about `T??`, one level down at the value. The annotation is written because
# without it `1` is an inference variable at the time the test is checked, and
# a hole agrees with everything.

def main():
    let n: Int be 1
    print(n?)
